  "description": "The side of the head. In front of the ear the superficial temporal artery ascends between the tragus and the condyle of the mandible, over the root of the zygomatic arch, and divides into frontal and parietal branches. The temporomandibular joint lies under the depression in front of the tragus, which deepens when the mouth opens. The parotid gland fills the space between the ear and the ramus of the mandible; the facial nerve runs forward through it and fans out over the zygomatic arch, across the cheek and along the lower border of the mandible, and the external carotid artery and the retromandibular vein lie deeper in the gland. Below the middle of the zygomatic arch the mandibular notch leads into the infratemporal fossa (maxillary artery, mandibular nerve). The facial artery crosses the lower border of the mandible at the anterior border of the masseter. Above the ear the temporalis lies on the thin temporal squama; behind the ear the mastoid is close under the skin, with the posterior auricular vessels in the groove behind the auricle.",
